{"id": "unknown-2026-06-12-010", "date": "2026-06-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 24, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "‘If I notice a woman being interrupted or overlooked, I intentionally bring the word back to her’", "content": "<p>This week Women in Solar+ Europe gives voice to Josefin Berg, Associate Director - Renewables Markets - Horizons at S&#38;P Global. She warns that the so-called “eclipse” moments, when women are interrupted or overshadowed in discussions, require vigilant, inclusive leadership that actively restores and amplifies overlooked voices.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/12/if-i-notice-a-woman-being-interrupted-or-overlooked-i-intentionally-bring-the-word-back-to-her/\">&#", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/12/if-i-notice-a-woman-being-interrupted-or-overlooked-i-intentionally-bring-the-word-back-to-her/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-12-011", "date": "2026-06-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 24, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Antaisolar unveils 80-meter multi-drive solar tracker", "content": "<p>At SNEC 2026, Antaisolar unveiled its upgraded TAI-Universal 2P multi-drive solar tracker with reinforced structure, up to 80 m spans and 60 m/s wind resistance.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/12/antaisolar-unveils-80-meter-multi-drive-solar-tracker/\">Antaisolar unveils 80-meter multi-drive solar tracker</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/12/antaisolar-unveils-80-meter-multi-drive-solar-tracker/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-12-012", "date": "2026-06-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 24, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Renewables-powered data centers feasible with sevenfold solar and wind overbuild, study finds", "content": "<p>A LUT University study finds that data centers could be powered continuously by intermittent renewables like wind and solar when paired with backup generation and demand-side flexibility. However, achieving firm supply would require major overbuild, significant curtailment, and careful siting to keep costs competitive with other baseload sources.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/12/renewables-powered-data-centers-feasible-with-sevenfold-solar-and-wind-overbuild-stu", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/12/renewables-powered-data-centers-feasible-with-sevenfold-solar-and-wind-overbuild-study-finds/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-12-013", "date": "2026-06-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 24, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Port of Valencia deploying PV on breakwaters", "content": "<p>The Port of Valencia is deploying solar panels on breakwaters as part of the EU-funded Renewport project to advance renewable energy in Mediterranean ports. The pilot system aims to validate the technical, economic, and environmental feasibility of large-scale vertical photovoltaics.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/12/valenciaport-instala-los-paneles-fotovoltaicos-de-su-fachada-vertical/\">Port of Valencia deploying PV on breakwaters</a> appeared first on <a href=\"", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/12/valenciaport-instala-los-paneles-fotovoltaicos-de-su-fachada-vertical/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "array-2026-06-12-014", "date": "2026-06-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 24, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": ["array"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Home cooling panel based on PV and waste cooking oil", "content": "<p>Researchers have designed a system that incorporates PV power generation, thermoelectric cooling, and latent heat storage using waste cooking oil. They have simulated an optimized it using an array of models. Results suggest that a single panel can deliver approximately 6–15 kWh/day of cooling. </p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/12/home-cooling-panel-based-on-pv-and-waste-cooking-oil/\">Home cooling panel based on PV and waste cooking oil</a> appeared first on <a hre", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/12/home-cooling-panel-based-on-pv-and-waste-cooking-oil/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-12-015", "date": "2026-06-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 24, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 1.0, "keywords": ["record"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "Hot weather and clear skies give Europe a bumper May", "content": "<p>In a new weekly update for <b>pv magazine</b>, Solcast, a DNV company, reports that Europe’s May weather was marked by a mid-month Arctic cold outbreak followed by a persistent heat dome that brought clear skies, record temperatures, and above-average solar irradiance across much of Central and Western Europe. While the blocking high boosted irradiance by up to 25% in some regions, cloudier conditions on its fringes left areas such as Scotland, Ireland, and Norway with below-average solar res", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/12/hot-weather-and-clear-skies-give-europe-a-bumper-may/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "daqo-2026-06-12-016", "date": "2026-06-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 24, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": ["daqo"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["expand"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Chinese PV Industry Brief: Daqo expands beyond polysilicon", "content": "<p>Daqo New Energy will invest CNY 6 billion ($835 million) to build a smart energy systems manufacturing base in Kunshan focused on advanced power equipment and storage solutions for AI data center applications.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/12/chinese-pv-industry-brief-daqo-expands-beyond-polysilicon/\">Chinese PV Industry Brief: Daqo expands beyond polysilicon</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/12/chinese-pv-industry-brief-daqo-expands-beyond-polysilicon/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-06-12-017", "date": "2026-06-12", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 6, "week": 24, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Chile releases bidding terms for first energy auction including storage", "content": "<p>hile’s CNE has set preliminary terms for the 2026/01 power supply tender, a technology-neutral process that nonetheless favors renewables by excluding high-emission fuels and enabling storage-backed bids. With time-of-day demand blocks and 15-year contracts, the structure is particularly supportive of photovoltaic and hybrid solar-plus-storage projects, especially for daytime and evening peak coverage.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/12/chile-releases-bidding-term", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/06/12/chile-releases-bidding-terms-for-first-energy-auction-including-storage/", "type": "rss"}]}
